                    {
                        "form_id": "3b767a0d-be2a-41e3-abe1-3cb1c81d7151",
                        "entry_id": "640d8b61-17f3-3450-bf65-443155c97a06",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "нечести́вцах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8d7f3b3e-4ff8-348a-934b-aae925fd9a55",
                        "entry_id": "640d8b61-17f3-3450-bf65-443155c97a06",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. нечестивый человек; тот, кто оскорбляет что-либо священное"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b256abe-506f-4dce-9fb0-54d07e74609b",
                                "sense_id": "8d7f3b3e-4ff8-348a-934b-aae925fd9a55",
                                "text": "― О, как должно было загреметь проклятие этого праведника и проклятие божие над главами этих нечестивцев!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bc0f056d-0f1a-4044-9604-07316aa03adf",
                                "sense_id": "8d7f3b3e-4ff8-348a-934b-aae925fd9a55",
                                "text": "― Блудники и нечестивцы, ― загремел пастор, ― вы, которым Господь Бог в неизреченной милости своей даровал труд, высшее благо Его, и отдых, чтобы прославлять Его совершенство, что делаете вы с вашими душами, за которые предал себя на распятие Иисус Христос?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "69b42e88-4f1b-488a-bf3b-d336f922d57f",
                                "sense_id": "8d7f3b3e-4ff8-348a-934b-aae925fd9a55",
                                "text": "― Вот нечестивец, который никогда не ходит в мечеть!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52811bd7-ed06-48dc-9cf5-f0c3bbbad6b2",
                                "sense_id": "8d7f3b3e-4ff8-348a-934b-aae925fd9a55",
                                "text": "Он глумился над мудрыми откровениями божественного Пифагора и противополагал ему нечестивца Эпикура, проклятого богами за свое неверие."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4870b5ea-30c3-3e92-80f8-2b56f7fa9500",
                        "entry_id": "640d8b61-17f3-3450-bf65-443155c97a06",
                        "glosses": [
                            "употребляется как порицающее или бранное слово"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b29fa30-a88b-41ab-a1b9-99bf4f597b17",
                                "sense_id": "4870b5ea-30c3-3e92-80f8-2b56f7fa9500",
                                "text": "― Прочь, ― сказал он, отталкивая Федора, ― прочь, нечестивец!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "258a29ee-86df-469a-86bd-20dd36b34116",
                                "sense_id": "4870b5ea-30c3-3e92-80f8-2b56f7fa9500",
                                "text": "― Где же ты пропадал столько дней, нечестивец?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "19732f79-f5f0-44b7-aac7-904cc8d73443",
                        "source_entry_id": "640d8b61-17f3-3450-bf65-443155c97a06",
                        "target_lang_word": "reprobate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "reprobate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29bb4e3f-528f-317d-831a-c5b7462674ab",
                                        "entry_id": "8c7b656f-cef1-384b-87bb-532df7e1c7f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rejected; cast off as worthless."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebb1b297-da27-4a7b-994e-cd1d441dad4c",
                                                "sense_id": "29bb4e3f-528f-317d-831a-c5b7462674ab",
                                                "text": "Reprobate silver shall men call them, because the Lord hath rejected them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "673fbf3a-d4b3-3efd-ab00-8fa10509ce3b",
                                        "entry_id": "8c7b656f-cef1-384b-87bb-532df7e1c7f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rejected by God; damned, sinful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6bec01d0-ab32-3310-a268-c565b9856bea",
                                        "entry_id": "8c7b656f-cef1-384b-87bb-532df7e1c7f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Immoral, having no religious or principled character."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01b0195e-cbb5-4008-8cea-54288bb27d7a",
                                                "sense_id": "6bec01d0-ab32-3310-a268-c565b9856bea",
                                                "text": "The reprobate criminal sneered at me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4a14cf5-f5cc-42d7-993a-6f24fc2c18b7",
                                                "sense_id": "6bec01d0-ab32-3310-a268-c565b9856bea",
                                                "text": "And strength, and art, are easily outdone / By spirits reprobate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "reprobate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31201c19-8c0a-3c45-88c3-0c4f49c41e59",
                                        "entry_id": "321a8369-1abf-3a99-b81b-8dc9aaf53fe0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One rejected by God; a sinful person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46607e4c-cbe1-4594-95f9-67847999f39d",
                                                "sense_id": "31201c19-8c0a-3c45-88c3-0c4f49c41e59",
                                                "text": "And the solitarines of man, which God had namely and principally orderd to prevent by mariage, hath no remedy, but lies under a worse condition then the loneliest single life; for in single life the absence and remotenes of a helper might inure him to expect his own comforts out of himselfe, or to seek with hope; but here the continuall sight of his deluded thoughts without cure, must needs be to him, if especially his complexion incline him to melancholy, a daily trouble and paine of losse in som degree like that which Reprobats feel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b91c72ea-4d28-3d40-827b-09a25c34e571",
                                        "entry_id": "321a8369-1abf-3a99-b81b-8dc9aaf53fe0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person with low morals or principles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "481946be-3446-4d5a-b03c-44a8c8f0d603",
                                                "sense_id": "b91c72ea-4d28-3d40-827b-09a25c34e571",
                                                "text": "I acknowledge myself for a reprobate, a villain, a traitor to the king."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed816229-a009-421b-81a8-d47bc99c9797",
                                                "sense_id": "b91c72ea-4d28-3d40-827b-09a25c34e571",
                                                "text": "[T]he young sinner took leave of Pen, and the club of the elder criminals, and sauntered into Blacquiere’s, an adjacent establishment, frequented by reprobates of his own age."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e38e951-a90b-4538-ade6-f5bc8c41e201",
                                                "sense_id": "b91c72ea-4d28-3d40-827b-09a25c34e571",
                                                "text": "\"Good morning, Mrs. Denny,\" he said. \"Wherefore this worried look on your face? Has that reprobate James been misbehaving himself?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04b6b137-a4af-4c03-a67f-c799cec8edbc",
                                                "sense_id": "b91c72ea-4d28-3d40-827b-09a25c34e571",
                                                "text": "West of here, it ascends to its viaduct where, 20 feet above the ground, the Westway seeks to emulate it; two scruffy reprobates shouldering their way through a not very pretty streetscape; the one a railway built by corporate buccaneers, the other a road constructed as part of a discredited plan to girdle London with motorways."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "reprobate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dfa654ca-337f-397c-843e-058e449da667",
                                        "entry_id": "dc3cfa80-063b-3531-a4e3-0756bccd4447",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To have strong disapproval of something; to reprove; to condemn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7155983-0f6a-44b9-a8cd-124f9ae898db",
                                                "sense_id": "dfa654ca-337f-397c-843e-058e449da667",
                                                "text": "Lord Rotheles allowed it was a very sufficient cause for returning soon, and reprobated all delays of letters, though he confessed to being a very idle correspondent;..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9751dc84-dd24-3c71-a38d-176c644b85ac",
                                        "entry_id": "dc3cfa80-063b-3531-a4e3-0756bccd4447",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of God: to abandon or reject, to deny eternal bliss."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9487862-7d0d-3898-976d-acf78f6229af",
                                        "entry_id": "dc3cfa80-063b-3531-a4e3-0756bccd4447",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To refuse, set aside."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
